window.docContents[111].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Game.StatementPq/#file-Computational___Specifications___Game___StatementPq":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Game › StatementPq.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by no headline theorem 606 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Listed with the statement files, but no headline theorem uses it. None of its declarations is in the closure of a headline theorem of either proof. Tier 1 lists it, as the closure report does: the report lists every statement file (defaultStatementFiles in scripts/TrustedClosure.lean). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\nDeclarations on this page (47)def cliPqPartyPathsdef cliPqPartyPathsOfdef cliPqReadBackdef cliPqDirInputsdef cliPqSig64def cliPqxdhDirBobBeforeAcceptstructure CliPartyStatedef cliPartyStateB0def cliPqLenOkdef cliPqSigsOfdef cliMapGameStatedef cliConfigSpkSdef cliOracleImplRstructure CliDriverStateabbrev CliDrvMTabbrev CliDrvMdef bhLiftCliMdef bhLiftClidef cliRunPureabbrev cliPqSendInpabbrev cliPqRecvInpdef cliPqAfterdef cliPqInitdef cliPqSenddef cliPqRecvdef cliPqReceivedef cliPqSchemedef cliPqInitMdef cliPqSendMdef cliPqRecvMdef cliPqReceiveMdef cliPqSchemeMdef cliDrvStartMdef cliDrvStartdef cliRunStdSMMdef cliRunStdSMdef cliStepLocalSMMdef cliStepLocalSMabbrev cliDrvSMMdef cliDrvSMabbrev cliDrvCtlMdef cliDrvCtlabbrev cliDrvImplMdef cliDrvImpldef cliIfacedef cliPqExpdef CliPqxdhAdvantage\n\n\n\nThe CLI security game on PQXDH directories with SPQRTrusted: the statement. Read with PqDir.lean (CliSpecPqxdh, encodeDir, pqInputs) and Run.lean (in LibsignalBinary/Specifications/SignalSession/), and Computational/Specifications/Game/StatementBinaryHarnessCore.lean. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Multi-session security game cliPqExp and distinguishing advantage CliPqxdhAdvantage for a libsignal command-line client run : CliRun executing PQXDH handshakes followed by SPQR-augmented Double Ratchet sessions. It instantiates the generic composed game G(Σ) (Computational/Specifications/Game/GenericGame.lean) at the CLI interface cliIface (Σ_bin), where each ACD19 secure-messaging (SM) step (init, send, recv) is one invocation of run on a party directory; the headline theorems instantiate run with the placed ARM64 semantics Placed.cliRunPlacedSig (LibsignalBinary/Specifications/SignalSession/CliBinaryPq.lean).At startDR, Alice's init <Bob> bundle runs on her initial encodeDir directory (pqInitInputs) and Bob's initial directory is encoded once from the KeyInd metadata (cliPartyStateB0). Across exit 0 invocations, Dir.cliPqAfter reads back all present party files along cliPqPartyPathsOf (cliPqReadBack) as the retained directory CliPartyState.dir passed to the next send or recv (cliPqDirInputs), recording sessions/<peer> in CliPartyState.bin.bytes; on corr-P, cliOracleImplR projects leaked state to CliPartyState.bin : BinState.DEV-CLI13 (formalization): Alice refuses every input whose first byte is 3. CliSpecPqxdh covers a pre-key message only when the session matches it or there is none, whereas Alice always holds the session she started; Dir.cliPqReceive refuses every byte-3-prefixed input to Alice before calling run. Effect: no claim about Alice receiving a pre-key message; honest Bob never sends one.DEV-CLI14 (formalization): explicit length gate; restricts the adversary. Dir.cliPqReceive refuses inputs of 2^32 bytes or more and canonical pre-key messages whose inner message has 2^32 - 2048 bytes or more (cliPqLenOk) before calling run, matching the injection filter bhInjOK. For plaintext length bound l < 10^6, no honest ciphertext reaches this threshold.DEV-CLI18 (formalization): exit 0 directory retention, non-zero exit rollback, and BinState leakage projection. Across exit 0 calls, CliPartyState.dir retains the full party directory snapshot (cliPqReadBack over cliPqPartyPathsOf), while corr-P leaks only CliPartyState.bin : BinState (matching modelIface's GhostState Bytes corruption surface rather than long-term identity or pre-key secret files). On any non-zero exit (exited c with c ≠ 0, aborted, or none), Dir.cliPqAfter returns none and leaves CliPartyState unchanged: under CliSpecPqxdh rejected calls leave party files untouched, allocation-failure aborts (DEV-CLI15) are accounted for separately in the CLI security bound, and mid-commit OS/I/O failures during sequential multi-file writes (EMFILE, ENOSPC, EIO, power loss) are out of scope (DEV-CLI4). Effect: out of scope (partial-write crash recovery on non-zero exit).\n\n\n\nParty directories and call inputs\n\ndef cliPqPartyPathsL77–86 ↗#Candidate relative file paths of a party directory, in the order emitted by encodeDir.\n\ndef cliPqPartyPathsOfL88–93 ↗#\n\ndef cliPqReadBackL95–99 ↗#Read back present party files along paths from fs, omitting missing paths (fs p = none) while keeping empty files (fs p = some []).\n\ndef cliPqDirInputsL101–108 ↗#Build CLI Inputs for cmd from a retained party directory dir, extra files, coin bytes, and stdin.\n\ndef cliPqSig64L110–112 ↗#Coerce bs to a 64-byte signature vector, defaulting to zeros when bs.length ≠ 64.\n\ndef cliPqxdhDirBobBeforeAcceptL114–126 ↗#Bob's initial PqParty directory before his first accept in instance bi, pinning Alice's identity key and installing the responder slot's signed pre-key, last-resort Kyber pre-key (with no seen base keys), and optional one-time pre-key, with no session.\n\nstructure CliPartyStateL128–134 ↗#Per-party state in a promoted CLI instance (DEV-CLI18): leaked BinState session record bin, fixed candidate directory paths paths, and retained directory snapshot dir.\n\ndef cliPartyStateB0L136–143 ↗#Bob's initial CliPartyState before his first accept in instance bi.\n\ndef cliPqLenOkL145–151 ↗#Ciphertext length gate (DEV-CLI14): requires shortCiphertext c (< 2 ^ 32 bytes) and inner payload length < 2 ^ 32 - 2048 on canonical tag-3 wires.\n\ndef cliPqSigsOfL153–158 ↗#Responder slot's (spkSig, pqspkSig) read from st.spkBundles (zero-filled if absent).\n\ndef cliMapGameStateL160–174 ↗#Map f : St' → St over the per-party states of an SM.GameState, keeping all metadata unchanged.\n\ndef cliConfigSpkSL176–187 ↗#Lift bhConfigSpkS (SM.ConfigR BinState Msg Bytes) to an arbitrary party-state type St.\n\ndef cliOracleImplRL189–199 ↗#R-game SM oracles running over internal party state St' and projecting corr-P leakage along proj : St' → St (DEV-CLI18).\n\nstructure CliDriverStateL201–204 ↗#Driver state of the CLI game, pairing ModelDriverState with per-instance CliPartyState SM states instGs (bi.gs caches the CliPartyState.bin projection).\n\nabbrev CliDrvMTL206–208 ↗#Monad transformer of the retained-directory CLI driver over M.\n\nabbrev CliDrvML210–211 ↗#\n\ndef bhLiftCliML213–219 ↗#Lift a BHDrvM computation into CliDrvMT, leaving instGs unchanged.\n\ndef bhLiftCliL221–226 ↗#\n\ndef cliRunPureL228–229 ↗#\n\nabbrev cliPqSendInpL231–232 ↗#\n\nabbrev cliPqRecvInpL234–235 ↗#\n\n\n\nSingle-call CLI scheme steps\n\ndef cliPqAfterL241–247 ↗#Extract (cliPqReadBack paths fs, sessions/<peer>, stdout) on exited 0, or none on any other outcome (DEV-CLI18).\n\ndef cliPqInitL249–257 ↗#Run Alice's init <Bob> bundle call with 192-byte tape t, returning her initial CliPartyState on exited 0.\n\ndef cliPqSendL259–268 ↗#Run send <peer> on s.dir with 64-byte send coins rs, updating s and returning stdout on exited 0, or (s, []) otherwise.\n\ndef cliPqRecvL270–284 ↗#Run recv <peer> on s.dir with 32-byte receive coins rc, updating s and parsing the inner SignalMessage header for (epoch, index) on exited 0.\n\ndef cliPqReceiveL286–311 ↗#Receive step of instance bi (DEV-CLI13, DEV-CLI14): enforces cliPqLenOk, refuses any wirePrekey-prefixed input to Alice, and checks partnered pre-key or whisper framing for Bob before invoking cliPqRecv.\n\ndef cliPqSchemeL313–320 ↗#SMSchemeR of promoted instance bi over retained CliPartyState directories.\n\ndef cliPqInitML322–325 ↗#\n\ndef cliPqSendML327–330 ↗#\n\ndef cliPqRecvML332–335 ↗#\n\ndef cliPqReceiveML337–359 ↗#\n\ndef cliPqSchemeML361–369 ↗#Monadic SMSchemeRM of promoted instance bi for an effectful runner runM.\n\nCLI game driver and security experiment\n\ndef cliDrvStartML373–431 ↗#Promote initiator session sid to a Double Ratchet instance: checks bhDrvGuard, evaluates testSession and revealSpkSk, runs Alice's init call via cliPqInitM, and commits the updated KeyIndState and new instance only if cliPqInitM succeeds.\n\ndef cliDrvStartL433–436 ↗#\n\ndef cliRunStdSMML438–467 ↗#Execute an admissible SM query q on promoted instance i via cliOracleImplRM, aligning gs.trans on post-accept Bob deliveries and projecting corr-P leakage to BinState.\n\ndef cliRunStdSML469–476 ↗#\n\ndef cliStepLocalSMML478–502 ↗#Pre-filter canonical pre-key wires to Alice and unpartnered or duplicate-in-transit wires to Bob before calling cliRunStdSMM.\n\ndef cliStepLocalSML504–511 ↗#\n\nabbrev cliDrvSMML513–535 ↗#Per-instance SM oracle handler checking bhDrvInstClean and pre-accept ikA corruption before dispatching to cliStepLocalSMM (or ext for external instances).\n\ndef cliDrvSML537–542 ↗#\n\nabbrev cliDrvCtlML544–548 ↗#\n\ndef cliDrvCtlL550–553 ↗#Control oracle handler dispatching startDR to cliDrvStart.\n\nabbrev cliDrvImplML555–565 ↗#Full composed-game oracle handler combining uniform coins, one-key real-HKDF bhDrvKeyInd, cliDrvCtlM, and cliDrvSMM.\n\ndef cliDrvImplL567–574 ↗#\n\n\n\ndef cliIfaceL578–590 ↗#CLI protocol interface Σ_bin of G(Σ) for runner run, model primitives modelPrims X W, plaintext byte length l, and epoch cap qep, with BinState corruption leakage and win predicate driverSomeInstanceWon.\n\ndef cliPqExpL592–598 ↗#Multi-session CLI security experiment G(Σ_bin) on PQXDH + SPQR party directories: runs A against cliIface, returning a uniform bit if allTestedSessionsFresh (modelPrims X W) fails at game end and (b' == b || driverSomeInstanceWon ds.toModelDriverState b) otherwise.\n\ndef CliPqxdhAdvantageL600–607 ↗#Distinguishing advantage 2 |Pr[cliPqExp … = true] - 1/2| (boolBias) of A in cliPqExp.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Game/StatementPq.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Game.StatementPq/#file-Computational___Specifications___Game___StatementPq"}});